[{"location":"api/#API-Reference","page":"API Reference","title":"API Reference","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"api/#DiffMatic.@matrix","page":"API Reference","title":"DiffMatic.@matrix","text":"@matrix(ids...)\n\nCreate one or more matrices. Example:\n\n@matrix A X\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"macro"},{"location":"api/#DiffMatic.@vector","page":"API Reference","title":"DiffMatic.@vector","text":"@vector(ids...)\n\nCreate one or more vectors. Example:\n\n@vector x y\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"macro"},{"location":"api/#DiffMatic.@scalar","page":"API Reference","title":"DiffMatic.@scalar","text":"@scalar(ids...)\n\nCreate one or more scalars. Example:\n\n@scalar a β\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"macro"},{"location":"api/#DiffMatic.derivative","page":"API Reference","title":"DiffMatic.derivative","text":"derivative(expr, wrt::Tensor)\n\nCompute the derivative of expr with respect to wrt. Example:\n\n@matrix A\n@vector x\n\nderivative(x' * x, x)\n\n# output\n\n2x₄\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#DiffMatic.gradient","page":"API Reference","title":"DiffMatic.gradient","text":"gradient(expr, wrt::Tensor)\n\nCompute the gradient of expr with respect to wrt. expr must be a scalar and wrt a vector. Example:\n\n@matrix A\n@vector x\n\ngradient(x' * A * x, x)\n\n# output\n\nx⁴A₄⁶ + A⁶⁵x₅\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#DiffMatic.jacobian","page":"API Reference","title":"DiffMatic.jacobian","text":"jacobian(expr, wrt::Tensor)\n\nCompute the jacobian of expr with respect to wrt. expr must be a column vector and wrt a vector. Example:\n\n@matrix A\n@vector x\n\njacobian(A * x, x)\n\n# output\n\nA¹₅\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#DiffMatic.hessian","page":"API Reference","title":"DiffMatic.hessian","text":"hessian(expr, wrt::Tensor)\n\nCompute the hessian of expr with respect to wrt. expr must be a scalar and wrt a vector. Example:\n\n@matrix A\n@vector x\n\nhessian(x' * A * x, x)\n\n# output\n\nA₇⁶ + A⁶₇\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"api/#DiffMatic.JuliaFunc","page":"API Reference","title":"DiffMatic.JuliaFunc","text":"JuliaFunc()\n\nJulia function that evaluates an expression in standard form.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"api/#DiffMatic.StdStr","page":"API Reference","title":"DiffMatic.StdStr","text":"StdStr()\n\nString format of an expression in standard form.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"api/#DiffMatic.to_std","page":"API Reference","title":"DiffMatic.to_std","text":"to_std(expr; format = StdStr())\n\nConvert the expression expr to standard notation.\n\nformat: Output format. Can be one of:\nStdStr: String format.\nJuliaFunc: Julia function.\n\nExamples:\n\n@matrix A\n@vector x\n\nto_std(gradient(x' * A * x, x))\n\n# output\n\n\"Aᵀx + Ax\"\n\nto_std(gradient(x' * A * x, x); format = JuliaFunc())\n\n# output\n\nquote\n    #= ... =#\n    function generated_function(A, x)\n        #= ... =#\n        #= ... =#\n        return transpose(A) * x + A * x\n    end\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"usage/#Differentiating-Matrix-Expressions","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"DiffMatic operates on expressions represented in Ricci-notation [1], which enables a precise treatment of tensor derivatives. After computing derivatives in Ricci-notation, the resulting expression can be converted back to standard notation. Derivatives written in standard matrix notation are compact and suitable for use with common libraries for linear algebra. DiffMatic can also generate code for evaluating derivatives directly.","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/#Matrices-and-Vectors-as-Tensors","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Matrices and Vectors as Tensors","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"Matrix expressions written in Julia syntax are automatically converted to Ricci-notation when using the types provided by DiffMatic. Matrices, vectors and scalars are created using the corresponding macros:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"using DiffMatic\n\n@matrix A B C\n@vector x y z\n@scalar a b c","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"All of the above variables are represented using the same type. The modes of a tensor can be seen by printing the variable:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"A\n\n# output\n\nA¹₂","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"Matrices have one upper and one lower index. Column vectors have one upper index:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"x\n\n# output\n\nx¹","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"Scalars have no indices.","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"note: Note\nAll elements are assumed to be real. Complex tensors are currently not supported.","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"note: Note\nIn Ricci-notation, and also Einstein notation, indices are usually written with letters. We use numbers for convenience.","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/#Creating-Tensor-Expressions","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Creating Tensor Expressions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"Many common functions are overloaded for the tensor type. This enables creationg of expressions in Ricci-notation using common standard Julia syntax. Tensor indices are automatically updated as needed.","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"A * x # standard matrix-vector multiplication\n\n# output\n\nA¹₄x⁴","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"The same index appearing both as an upper and as a lower index indicates a contraction over that index. Multiplying with a scalar does not result in a contraction:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"c * A\n\n# output\n\ncA¹₂","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"Supported operators and functions when creating expressions:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"Basic operators +, -, ', *, ^, abs, sin, cos and log\nElement-wise operators sin., cos., abs., .*, .^ and log.\nVector 1-norm and 2-norm can be computed with LinearAlgebra.norm(..., 1) and LinearAlgebra.norm(..., 2)\nSums of vectors can be computed with sum.\nMatrix traces can be computed with LinearAlgebra.tr.","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"See Creating Expressions for more examples.","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/#Computing-Derivatives","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Computing Derivatives","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"Matrix derivatives are computed on expressions in Ricci-notation directly. DiffMatic provides specialized functions for computing gradients, Jacobians and Hessians respectively.","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"gradient and hessian require a scalar as input:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"expr = 2 * x' * A * B * x\n\ng = gradient(expr, x) # The second argument denotes the differentiation variable.\n\n# output\n\n2A₄⁶B₆⁸x⁴ + 2B₆⁷x₇A⁸⁶","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"H = hessian(expr, x)\n\n# output\n\n2A₉⁶B₆⁸ + 2B₆₉A⁸⁶","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"jacobian requires a column vector as input:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"J = jacobian(x' * x * A * x, x)\n\n# output\n\nx₃x³A¹₆ + 2A¹₅x⁵x₆","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"See Derivatives in Standard Notation for more examples.","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/#Converting-Tensor-Expression-to-Standard-Notation","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Converting Tensor Expression to Standard Notation","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"An expression in Ricci-notation can be converted back to standard notation using to_std. DiffMatic can output a standard expression in string format or as a Julia function.","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/#String-Output","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"String Output","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"An expression can be converted to standard matrix notation and retrieved as a string by passing StdStr as a keyword argument to to_std:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"to_std(J; format = StdStr())\n\n# output\n\n\"xᵀxA + 2Axxᵀ\"","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"Special notation used in the output:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"\"⊙\": Element-wise multiplication.\n\"diag(x)\": Diagonal matrix with \"x\" on the diagonal.\n\"vec(1)\": Vector consisting of 1:s.\n\"sgn(x)\": The signum function applied element-wise.\n\"tr(X)\": Trace of the matrix \"X\".\n\"abs(x)\": Element-wise absolute value of \"x\".","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/#Julia-Function","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Julia Function","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"A Julia function is generated by passing JuliaFunc as a keyword argument to to_std. The function is returned in the form of an expression:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"to_std(g; format = JuliaFunc())\n\n# output\n\nquote\n    #= ... =#\n    function (B, A, x)\n        #= ... =#\n        #= ... =#\n        return 2 * (transpose(B) * (transpose(A) * x)) + 2 * ((A * B) * x)\n    end\nend","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"The generated function can be compiled using eval:","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"g_fun = eval(to_std(g; format = JuliaFunc()))\n\nAn = Float64[1 1 1; 2 2 2; 3 3 3]\nBn = Float64[4 4 4; 5 5 5; 6 6 6]\nxn = Float64[1; 1; 1]\n\ng_fun(An, Bn, xn)\n\n# output\n\n3-element Vector{Float64}:\n 270.0\n 360.0\n 450.0","category":"page"},{"location":"usage/","page":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","title":"Differentiating Matrix Expressions","text":"S. Laue, M. Mitterreiter and J. Giesen. Computing Higher Order Derivatives of Matrix and Tensor Expressions. In: Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems, Vol. 31 (Curran Associates, Inc., 2018).\n\n\n\n","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Examples","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/#Creating-Variables","page":"Examples","title":"Creating Variables","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"using LinearAlgebra: tr, norm\nusing DiffMatic\n\n@matrix A B C\n@vector x y z\n@scalar c","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Creating-Expressions","page":"Examples","title":"Creating Expressions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/#Matrix-Multiplication-and-Transpose","page":"Examples","title":"Matrix Multiplication and Transpose","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = x' * A * x\n\n# output\n\nx₄A⁴₅x⁵","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = x' * A' * x\n\n# output\n\nx₄A₅⁴x⁵","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = A * B * x\n\n# output\n\nA¹₅B⁵₇x⁷","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Hadamard/Element-wise-Product","page":"Examples","title":"Hadamard/Element-wise Product","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = A .* B .* C\n\n# output\n\nA¹₂B¹₂C¹₂","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = x .* y .* z\n\n# output\n\nx¹y¹z¹","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Powers-and-Element-wise-Powers","page":"Examples","title":"Powers and Element-wise Powers","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = (x' * A * x)^2\n\n# output\n\n(x₄A⁴₅x⁵).^2","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = (x .* y).^2\n\n# output\n\n(x¹y¹).^2","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = (A * x).^2\n\n# output\n\n(A¹₄x⁴).^2","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Trigonometric-Functions","page":"Examples","title":"Trigonometric Functions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = sin.(A * x)\n\n# output\n\nsin(A¹₄x⁴)","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = cos(x' * x)\n\n# output\n\ncos(x₃x³)","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Absolute-Value","page":"Examples","title":"Absolute Value","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = abs.(A * x)\n\n# output\n\n|A¹₄x⁴|","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = abs(x' * x)\n\n# output\n\n|x₃x³|","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Sum-of-a-vector","page":"Examples","title":"Sum of a vector","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = sum(x .* y)\n\n# output\n\nx¹y¹1₁","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = sum(A * x)\n\n# output\n\nA¹₄x⁴1₁","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Log-and-element-wise-log","page":"Examples","title":"Log and element-wise log","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = log(x' * y)\n\n# output\n\nlog(x₃y³)","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = log.(x)' * y\n\n# output\n\nlog(x₃)y³","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Vector-Norms","page":"Examples","title":"Vector Norms","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = norm(A * x, 2)\n\n# output\n\n((A¹₄x⁴).^21₁).^(1/2)","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = norm(A * x, 1)\n\n# output\n\n|A¹₄x⁴|1₁","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Matrix-Trace","page":"Examples","title":"Matrix Trace","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = tr(A)\n\n# output\n\nA²₂","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"expr = tr(A*B*B'*C)\n\n# output\n\nB⁵₇A¹₅B₉⁷C⁹₁","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Derivatives-in-Standard-Notation","page":"Examples","title":"Derivatives in Standard Notation","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/#Gradient","page":"Examples","title":"Gradient","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient(tr(x * x'), x))\n\n# output\n\n\"2x\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient(tr(x * x'), x))\n\n# output\n\n\"2x\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient((x .* y)' * x, x))\n\n# output\n\n\"2(x ⊙ y)\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient((x - y)' * x, x))\n\n# output\n\n\"2x - y\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient(sin(tr(x * x')), x))\n\n# output\n\n\"cos(xᵀx)2x\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient(abs(x' * x), x))\n\n# output\n\n\"sgn(xᵀx)2x\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient(log.(x)'*x, x))\n\n# output\n\n\"vec(1) + log(x)\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient(2 * sum(cos.(A * x + y)), x))\n\n# output\n\n\"(-2)Aᵀsin(Ax + y)\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient((x' * A * x) ^ (-2), x))\n\n# output\n\n\"(-2)(xᵀAᵀx)⁻³(Aᵀx + Ax)\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient(((A .* (B .* C)) * C * x)' * x, x))\n\n# output\n\n\"(B ⊙ C ⊙ A)Cx + Cᵀ(Bᵀ ⊙ Cᵀ ⊙ Aᵀ)x\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(gradient(sum((A .* B) * C * x), x))\n\n# output\n\n\"Cᵀ(Aᵀ ⊙ Bᵀ)vec(1)\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/#Jacobian","page":"Examples","title":"Jacobian","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(jacobian(A * x, x))\n\n# output\n\n\"A\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(jacobian(A' * x, x))\n\n# output\n\n\"Aᵀ\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(jacobian(sin.(A * x + y), x))\n\n# output\n\n\"diag(cos(Ax + y))A\"","category":"page"},{"location":"examples/","page":"Examples","title":"Examples","text":"to_std(jacobian(((A .* B) * C * x)' * x * x, x))\n\n# output\n\n\"xᵀCᵀ(Aᵀ ⊙ Bᵀ)xI + x(xᵀCᵀ(Aᵀ ⊙ Bᵀ) + xᵀ(A ⊙ B)C)\"","category":"page"},{"location":"#DiffMatic.jl","page":"Quick Start","title":"DiffMatic.jl","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"DiffMatic is a package for computing derivatives of matrix expressions, also known as matrix calculus. Provided are functions for computing gradients, Jacobians, Hessians and general matrix derivatives.","category":"page"},{"location":"#Installation","page":"Quick Start","title":"Installation","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"Installation from the general registry:","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"using Pkg; Pkg.add(\"DiffMatic\")","category":"page"},{"location":"#Usage","page":"Quick Start","title":"Usage","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"Expressions are constructed from Julia syntax.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"Creating a matrix and a column vector:","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"using DiffMatic\n\n@matrix A\n@vector x","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"Creating an expression:","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"expr = x' * A * x\n\n# output\n\nx₄A⁴₅x⁵","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"The variable expr now contains an internal representation of the expression x' * A * x.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"Compute the gradient and the Hessian with respect to the column vector x.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"g = gradient(expr, x)\nH = hessian(expr, x)","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"Convert the gradient into standard notation using to_std:","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"to_std(g)\n\n# output\n\n\"Aᵀx + Ax\"","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"Convert the the Hessian into standard notation:","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"to_std(H)\n\n# output\n\n\"Aᵀ + A\"","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"Jacobians can be computed with jacobian:","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"to_std(jacobian(A * x, x))\n\n# output\n\n\"A\"","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"The function derivative can be used to compute arbitrary derivatives.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"using LinearAlgebra: tr\n\nto_std(derivative(tr(A), A))\n\n# output\n\n\"I\"","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"The function to_std will throw an exception when given an expression that that cannot be converted to standard notation:","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Quick Start","title":"Quick Start","text":"to_std(derivative(A, A))\n\n# output\n\nERROR: DomainError","category":"page"}]
